# Entity detail patterns

Full guide: `docs/entity-detail-design-patterns.md`. Reference UIs: customer, vehicle, quotation, job order, invoice, and payment details.

## Layout

- Use `EntityDetailLayout` (`header` + main tabs/tables + sticky `sidebar`).
- Do **not** add a third column for back navigation.

## Header

- `backHref` → circular chevron left of the title (listing URL, not `router.back()`).
- Identity facts (status, type, member-since) → `MetadataPill` in the header only.
- Actions → `TableRowActionsMenu` (`...`) only; no standalone Edit/Add buttons.
- Form-only screens without a detail page (e.g. product create/edit) use the same circular back on `PageHeader` via `backHref`.

## Overview sidebar

- `EntityDetailField`: label left, value right; empty → `-`.
- Values: medium slate gray (`text-slate-600`), not bold black.
- Only real/editable fields (or real system values). No placeholders (advisor, tags, secondary phone, etc.).
- Never repeat header pills. Never duplicate counts that belong in a tab.
- Hide whole sections when they have nothing useful.

## Tables (every related-record tab)

- Always `EntityDataTable` + `FilterBar` (`SearchInput` + `NativeSelect`s).
- Lean columns (about 4–6). Fold secondary labels under the primary cell (e.g. type under document #).
- If the only action is view → **clickable row**, no Actions column.
- Nested detail → expandable row + `colSpan` panel (not a separate list).
- Keep equal cell padding on first/last columns (don’t flush content to the edges).
- Empty cells → `-`. Empty states for no data and for no filter matches.

## Checklist

Back · overflow actions · no sidebar dupes · table + filters · lean columns · clickable view rows · `-` empties · edge padding
